{
  "_notes": [
    "Map for Atari Superman and Hercules.",
    "Free Play (DIP SW A6) not mirrored in RAM/NVRAM.",
    "game_over is 0x007D, the game-in-progress flag, read inverted: 0x00 in attract, 0x10 for every",
    "sample of a game including between balls, 0x00 again the moment the game ends. Measured on",
    "superman from a 389-sample recording of live RAM (2026-09-11) spanning attract, one three-ball",
    "game and attract again; correct in every sample. 0x2B (02 attract / 03 in play) says the same",
    "thing; 0x2C/0x2D (30/0F) drop to zero between balls, so they mark a ball in play, not a game.",
    "The earlier candidate 0x00A0 is an attract animation: 0x80 with brief 0x00 blips every few",
    "seconds throughout attract and 0x00 during a game. Read as a game-over flag it reported a",
    "finished game on every blink of an untouched machine.",
    "The ball at 0x005A does not return to 0 after a game: it steps to one past the last ball (4 on",
    "a 3-ball game) and stays there until the next game starts, so consumers cannot rely on the",
    "ball clearing to detect the end."
  ],
